WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.243 --> 00:00:03.837
♪♪

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.739
-In 1973,
The Allman Brothers Band

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.174
was one of the most
prominent touring rock acts

00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:10.276
in the country.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.312
Fresh off the release of
their third album,

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.880
they returned to the studio in
search of their next sound.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.584
It was during this time that
founding member Dickey Betts

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:21.621
wrote what would soon become
one of their biggest hits.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:25.358
"Ramblin' Man" quickly became
an American classic,

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.460
peaking at number 2 on
the Billboard Hot 100 chart

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.863
and earning its place as one of

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.398
the greatest rock songs
of all time.

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:36.169
But America never heard
its first draft...until now.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:40.139
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:45.211
♪♪

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:50.350
-♪ Lord, I was born
a ramblin' man ♪

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.787
♪ Tryin' to make a livin' and
doin' the best I can ♪

00:00:55.288 --> 00:01:01.160
♪ And I was born in the
back seat of a Greyhound bus ♪

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:05.565
♪ I was born ramblin' man ♪

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:10.503
♪ Like I said,
I was born in a Greyhound ♪

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:11.938
♪ The people
on the bus were like,

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:15.641
"Hey, what's that noise?" ♪

00:01:15.641 --> 00:01:17.910
♪ Some guy yelled, "I think that

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:21.014
a lady's giving birth ♪

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:25.651
♪ In the back seat
of this Greyhound bus ♪

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:29.188
♪ The bus driver screamed,
"Wait, should I pull over?" ♪

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:35.395
♪ A few people on board said,
"No, just drive ♪

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.164
♪ But a couple
other people said,

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.267
"You gotta park this bus" ♪

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.971
♪ The driver did not
park the bus ♪

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:50.476
♪♪

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:55.581
-♪ I knew you were born
a ramblin' man ♪

00:01:55.581 --> 00:02:00.887
♪ But I didn't know about the
bus birth till just now ♪

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:05.758
♪ I'd kinda prefer
we sing about anything else ♪

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:10.930
♪ But I'm also weirdly curious ♪

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:15.735
-♪ Well, if you've got
a question, you can ask it ♪

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:20.806
♪ And I'll try to remember
details from that 'Hound ♪

00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:23.476
-♪ I don't even
know where to start ♪

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.378
♪ I guess,
how much did you weigh? ♪

00:02:26.378 --> 00:02:30.617
-♪ Somewhere between
6 and 20 pounds ♪

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:36.222
-♪ 20 pounds
is too big for a baby ♪

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:40.760
♪ I wanna say
the average is like 8 ♪

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:46.899
-♪ Well, it ain't like they had
a scale on that bus ♪

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:50.269
♪ That was just an estimate ♪

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:56.175
♪♪

00:02:56.175 --> 00:03:00.679
-♪ Now, did your mother
name you on that Greyhound? ♪

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:06.285
-♪ Well, she named me after
the driver of that bus ♪

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:08.554
♪ His name was Nicky Bus ♪

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:11.224
-♪ But your name is
Dickey Betts ♪

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:16.228
-♪ That's 'cause she wrote
the name down wrong ♪

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:21.601
-♪ Dickey Betts was born
on a Greyhound ♪

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.104
♪ Dickey Betts
was born on a Greyhound ♪

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:31.644
♪ Dickey Betts was born
on a Greyhound bus ♪

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:35.748
♪ Dickey Betts
was born on a bus ♪

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.785
♪♪

